  <text>
      <body>
         <entry xml:id="alwe-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">אלווי</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">ʾlwwy</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic">alwe</pron>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="pos">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen">f.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <form type="inflected">
               <orth type="inflected" xml:lang="jpa">אלווס</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb">ʾlwws</orth>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="num">pl.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="alwe-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>aloe wood</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>ἀλόη</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <lbl>pl.</lbl>
                  <quote>ἀλόης</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>ר' אמר שלשה, ברוש ברתה, תדהר אדרה, תאשור פיקסוס, למה קורא אותו תאשור, רבנין אמ' שהוא מאושר מכולן, הוסיפו עליהם עוד שלשה, אלונין ערמונין אלמוגין, אלונין בלוטין, ערמונין דולבי, אלמוגים 
                     <app>
                        <lem>אלווס</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox1">דולוס</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox2">דולבוס</rdg>
                     </app>.</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">15,1</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">I 136: 4</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">פיקסוס</ref>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>Rabbi said: They are but three [trees]: berosh is the “beratah” (cypress); tidhar is the “adarah”-tree, teʾashur is the box-tree. Why is it called teʾashur? The Rabbis say: Because it is the most valuable (“meʾushar”) of all. To these they added another three: “alonin”, “armonin”, “almugin”. “Alonin” are oak-trees; “armonin” are plane-trees, and “almugin” are aloe-trees. (Freedman / Simon I 119-120)</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">yKet 7,9 [993: 19]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">אלוים</term>)</note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>Only pl. See <bibl type="modern">Krauss, LW II 51</bibl>. The Pl. in Yerushalmi shall be read as <term xml:lang="jpa">אלויס</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">ʾlwys</term> fitting the pl. in Gr., but see Sokoloff. For Syr. <term xml:lang="syc">ܐܠܘܐ</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">ʾlwʾ</term> see <bibl type="modern">Sokoloff, SL 48a</bibl>. For the reading of Ox 1 see <bibl type="modern">Krauss, LW II 190b</bibl> and <bibl type="modern">Sperber, Cards</bibl> for further information.</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Sokoloff, DJPA</title>
                  <citedRange>34ab</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
